{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender scripting interface customization blender scripting interface customization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","fileName":"Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Scripting Interface Customization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Scripting Environment]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender scripting interface customization blender scripting interface customization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","fileName":"Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Scripting Interface Customization","heading":"Blender Scripting Interface Customization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender's areas are modular: an area can change editor type, be divided, or be combined with another area. A scripting layout can therefore place a 3D Viewport, Text Editor, Interactive Console, Command Log, and Properties editor together according to the current task.\n\nThis configurability turns the interface into part of the development method. Multiple Text Editors help separate a main script from utilities, while a second display can dedicate more room to code or diagnostics. The layout does not create separate data contexts; its editors remain different views onto the same Blender scene.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender scripting interface customization blender scripting interface customization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","fileName":"Blender Scripting Interface Customization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Scripting Interface Customization","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}